From f915d6ed819c37a5105d215797c8e2bb8d3e0fdc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 16:35:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Update check: a beta channel behind an opt-in; QoS page:
 retire the Weighted-class prose

The update manifest may now carry a second line per model and variant,
MODEL#VARIANT-beta#X.Y.Z#url#sha#size, written by the Dev-branch publish.
reaper_webs_update.sh reads it only when reaper_fwbeta=1 (new key,
defaults.c, default 0) and offers a beta only to a router that is already on
the newest stable release and only when the beta carries a HIGHER number than
that stable - a beta with the stable's own number is never offered. A beta
offer is marked in webs_state_channel: the Firmware page and the dashboard
badge label it, reaper_webs_note.sh fetches the -beta note first. Firmware
before this commit anchors its grep on "VARIANT#" and never sees the line.

Reaper_Firmware.asp gains the Beta Channel switch (saveNvram reaper_fwbeta)
and the label; RFWU_54-57 in all 25 packs, translated.

Reaper_QoS.asp: the hint under the class list and the "Priority vs Weighted"
explainer described a scheduler mode removed in v2.5.4. RQOS_28 is cut to its
Priority sentence in every pack; the explainer block is gone from the page
(the RQOS_51-54 and RQOS_95 keys stay, unused).

Gates: reaper_static_checks 11/11 (new check fw-beta-channel), langcheck 0,
csrfcheck 0, node --check on both pages, dicts lockstep 6867; the check
script's decision matrix (11 cases) run offline against fake nvram/wget.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
